<title>UK: U.K. Intervention Board details EU sugar sales.</title>
<headline>U.K. Intervention Board details EU sugar sales.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>A total 16,000 tonnes of current series white sugar received export rebates of a maximum 43.521 European Currency Units (Ecus) per 100 kilos at Wednesday's European Union (EU) tender, the U.K. Intervention Board said.</p>
<p>Traders in France received the total allotment, it added.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8072</p>
